-- title:
--   Cokernel of π_* on Cartier modules has rank rank dρ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ a perfect field of characteristic $p$, and let $d$ be a natural number. Let $\Psi,\Psi'$ be $d$-dimensional formal group laws over $k$ in the sense of [`MvFormalGroup`](def/MvFormalGroup_BasicV2.html#L15) (a $d$-tuple of power series in $2d$ variables with vanishing constant coefficients, linear terms $X_i+Y_i$, and the associativity identity), both assumed commutative in the sense of `IsComm`. Let $\pi$ be a homomorphism $\Psi\to\Psi'$ and $\rho$ a homomorphism $\Psi'\to\Psi^{(p)}$, where $\Psi^{(p)}$ is `Ψ.map (frobenius k p)`, the formal group law obtained by raising all coefficients of $\Psi$ to the $p$-th power; here a homomorphism is a $d$-tuple of power series in $d$ variables with vanishing constant coefficients satisfying the usual substitution identity. Assume that the composite $\rho\circ\pi$, formed by substituting the series of $\pi$ into those of $\rho$, has $i$-th component $X_i^{\,p}$ for every $i$, and that $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ modulo the ideal generated by the components of $\rho$ is a finite-dimensional $k$-module. Write $M(\Psi)$, $M(\Psi')$ for the Cartier modules `CartierModule p Ψ`, `CartierModule p Ψ'` (tuples of power series in variables indexed by $\mathbb N$ with zero constant coefficients, compatible with the Witt addition law via the group law), and let $\pi_*$ denote `CartierModule.map π`. Then the $W(k)/(p)$-module $\bigl(M(\Psi')/p\,M(\Psi')\bigr)$ modulo the span of the classes of $\pi_*g$, $g\in M(\Psi)$, admits a basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}$ of the rank of the matrix [`MvFormalGroup.linearPart ρ.toPowerSeries`](def/MvFormalGroup_BasicV2.html#L359), the $d\times d$ matrix of coefficients of $X_j$ in $\rho_i$; in particular the conclusion asserts the existence of such a basis rather than producing a distinguished one.
--
--   This is the Cartier-theoretic computation of the cokernel of $\pi_*$ for a factorisation $\rho\circ\pi=\mathrm{Frob}_\Psi$ of the Frobenius of a commutative formal group law: the cokernel is a $k$-vector space of dimension equal to the rank of the differential $d\rho$. It feeds the results [`MvFormalGroup.CartierModule.nonempty_basis_quotient_span_range_map_of_finrank_eq_pow`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.CartierModule.nonempty_basis_quotient_span_range_map_of_finrank_eq_pow) and [`MvFormalGroup.CartierModule.length_quotient_range_mapLinear_eq_of_finrank_eq_pow`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.CartierModule.length_quotient_range_mapLinear_eq_of_finrank_eq_pow), where the kernel algebra of $\rho$ is assumed of $k$-dimension a power of $p$.
